          "id": "prt_msg_ses_33_04_02",
          "sessionID": "ses_33",
          "messageID": "msg_ses_33_04",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "That test isn't testing `sanitizeTopicTitle` at all — `jest.mock` replaces the real function with a stub, and `mockReturnValue('clean title')` just tells the stub what to return. The `expect` is checking your own stub against the value you told it to return, so it can't fail. Coverage shows the line as \"covered\" because the call happened, not because the real logic ran. Drop the `jest.mock` for this function and call the real implementation — mocking is for the dependencies *it* calls, not the function you're testing."
        },
        {
          "id": "prt_msg_ses_33_04_03",
          "sessionID": "ses_33",
